ns and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-5,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-10,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541066 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d37bcc4-0c9f-508d-8122-95d6a1703d93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541066 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =2{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =2(-5-10) \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1071 "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<0, \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66ff7371-5323-5876-b071-49b4ca2a6463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541090 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(0,\\pi )\\times ((-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0)\\cup (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =((0,\\pi )\\times (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0))\\cup ((0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541167 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2a278359-e48b-574c-8558-aec54e3db4bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541167 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186380894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541192 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541192 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "76b49b70-28b4-5fb8-b154-916347e649e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541192 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541198 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541198 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "893db046-3a6d-56c7-8f63-bc9d855915b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541198 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186380873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541219 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541219 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca77b050-7163-5e44-bed7-5cbfe6365a13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541219 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541220 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541220 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd03560a-f875-5516-bfa6-d69e8b5f5aca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541220 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129872 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
